id: ops-evidence-expiry
title: Invalidate only operational claims whose evidence expires or whose scoped versions change
description: "Acceptance: attach explicit freshness and scope requirements to accepted health, coverage and recovery receipts. Changing a relevant package or backend version invalidates only affected claims. Unavailable evidence never becomes a pass. Deliver typed SDK, agent-sized TOON/JSON CLI, refusals with remedies, docs, non-git real-tracker validation and npm/Bun CI release gates."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-22T16:06:35.472Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T19:06:13.660Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Changing the relevant package or backend version invalidates only affected claims; Unavailable evidence never becomes a pass; Accepted health, coverage and recovery receipts have explicit freshness and population scope requirements"
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T16:06:40.798Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: pinned core SDK assurance owns declarations, scope validation, assertion evaluation and verified durable verdict history (listAssuranceVerdicts); pm-review/src/round.ts gates exact PR heads and completed checks. pm-context receipts track context usage. pm-ops assurance.ts refuses source-stale lcov and backend-capabilities.ts audits list/get/schema contracts. None evaluates retained operational health/coverage/recovery evidence against cross-package and backend version scopes plus wall-clock freshness. Plan: bind explicit policies to core immutable assertion receipts and use the SDK verified verdict reader; no parallel assurance store, contract evaluator, Git dependency or tracker mutation on evaluation. Published CLI latest verified as 2026.10.22; preserve the repo SDK pin 2026.10.17."
  "2026-10-22T16:14:29.378Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: exact core gate/tree/time/assertion attachment, core population scope, exclusive TTL boundary and explicit relevant identity map. Directory audit uses listAssuranceVerdicts, readHistorySnapshot and verifyHistoryRecordHash; core scope semantics are reused with an additional boundary guard because the pinned assertion validator accepts an unknown scope kind. Read-only non-git tests compare every tracker byte and remove Git from PATH. Targeted expiry and renderer suites pass 16/16. Default diagnostic output bounds rows and preserves full counts; ok is the authoritative diagnostic predicate, consistent with ops capabilities. No hosted access or dependency bump."
  "2026-10-22T16:18:19.441Z",codex-agent,"Real-data validation: read-only non-git export of public main 3546c385e30d9914ab8a5690ccee7842ca38a7d9 contained 148 items, 6 types, 309 files and zero core gate verdicts; SDK warnings 0. Three claims stayed unavailable (evidence_missing) before and after changing all scoped versions; 0 fresh, 0 revalidate, 3 unavailable. Compact JSON 882 bytes. All tracker bytes unchanged. Positive controls use separate real initialized scratch trackers with SDK-evaluated sealed verdicts. Focused expiry coverage is 100/100/100/100. Behavioral revert proofs: bypassing version invalidation fails selective regression (0 pass/1 fail); bypassing hash refusal fails tamper regression (0 pass/1 fail); source restored. SDK listAssuranceVerdicts reads durable receipts; separate SDK hash checks establish record integrity, not global authentication."
  "2026-10-22T16:19:52.602Z",codex-agent,"Local acceptance: 18/18 targeted expiry and renderer regressions pass, including actual installed CLI TOON/JSON parsing, typed invalid-option exit 2 and no Git executable. Typecheck, test typecheck, build, lint, zero-duplication and docstring checks pass at unchanged thresholds. Focused expiry module coverage is four 100 percent dimensions. Full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI because the shared host is saturated. Boundary notes: consumers must include every relevant version identity; pure remote evaluation trusts authenticated caller receipts; history search is bounded to newest 1000 verdicts. No operational health/coverage/recovery certification is claimed from missing public receipts."
  "2026-10-22T16:22:23.149Z",codex-agent,"Review-ready PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/192 . CI release matrix started at implementation commit f0b17f3f0dc9e9c80938478692bfa419b86414db: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/39813347953 . Local linked tests pass 18/18 with zero skips. Strict tracker health passes with an isolated home and no global Git configuration; the ordinary environment reports an unrelated global pm-github 2026.10.22 versus pinned host 2026.10.17 skew. Changelog generation/check pass. Awaiting CI before final handoff."
  "2026-10-22T16:27:27.849Z",codex-agent,"CI evidence at implementation commit f0b17f3f0dc9e9c80938478692bfa419b86414db: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/39813347953 passed all 4 jobs, including Windows consumers on Node 22 and 26. npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed on Node 22 and 26: per gate 1410 tests, 1408 passed, 0 failed, 2 existing opt-in configured-repository checks skipped. All 4 coverage dimensions are 100 percent across 32 measured sources. Targeted new/renderer tests pass 18/18, zero skips. Duplication 0 percent; 268 documented declarations; production audit zero vulnerabilities. CodeQL passed. Reviewer evidence is unavailable: automatic reviews disabled or quota/subscription limited, not approval. Acceptance criteria are evidenced; final evidence-only commit will get its own CI run before handoff. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification and closure."
  "2026-10-22T19:03:17.943Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched every unresolved thread and all comments, plus latest CodeRabbit review at 5eabf51. One thread PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M6vVDtP is valid: the no-Git subprocess static ESM import uses a raw absolute path, which is not portable on Windows. No outside-diff findings or pagination gaps. Remote head is pulled and current main is already an ancestor (2 branch commits, 0 missing main commits), so no merge is required. Plan: convert the import specifier through pathToFileURL and exercise a real temporary module filename containing a space and hash, so reverting only the URL conversion fails on POSIX as well as Windows. Review the entire PR diff for other module-specifier/path confusions, keep existing operational evidence, rebuild dist and use unchanged npm/Bun CI release gates. Do not reply to or resolve review threads."
  "2026-10-22T19:05:07.035Z",codex-agent,"Fixed valid review thread PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M6vVDtP: no-Git subprocess module imports now use file URLs, and the real temporary probe entry includes a space and hash to exercise URI escaping on POSIX too. Revert proof: replacing only pathToFileURL(probeEntry).href with the raw probeEntry, preserving the fixture and assertions, fails the focused command (0 pass, 1 fail, ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND, exit 1); restored conversion passes (1 pass, 0 fail, 0 skips). Command: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"read-only SDK and CLI dispatch\" test/evidence-expiry.test.ts. Whole-PR self-review found the other generated ESM shim already uses pathToFileURL; all remaining added path arguments are Node entrypoints or filesystem inputs, not module specifiers. No other same-class defect in the PR diff. No outside-diff findings. Existing public-tracker operational evidence is retained without repeating completed work."
  "2026-10-22T19:06:13.660Z",codex-agent,"Review-fix local validation: npm ci passed (204 audited packages, zero vulnerabilities). Linked command node --test test/evidence-expiry.test.ts test/renderer-ownership.test.ts passed 18/18, zero skips, zero timeouts. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run build, npm run lint, npm run duplication and npm run docstring passed at unchanged thresholds. Duplication remains zero clone pairs; 268 declarations documented across 32 source files. Rebuilt tracked dist is byte-identical because the fix is confined to the test probe. The full npm/Bun release matrix will run in CI under the original saturated-host policy before final handoff."
